---
import UseCase from "../../layouts/UseCase.astro"
import Beat from "../../components/Beat.astro"
import Term from "../../components/Term.astro"
import { installerBase, previewDomain } from "../../site"

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What can an agent's token do?",
    a: "Only what you put in it: which machines, which actions, for how long. Ask <code>pb policy explain</code> before you hand it over.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does the agent see my secrets?",
    a: "It never needs a value in its prompt, its arguments or a file. <code>pb env run -- cmd</code> puts the values in that one command's environment.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I see what an agent did?",
    a: "The audit log records each action with the token that did it, the machine, and whether it was allowed. Record its terminal to see every step.",
  },
  {
    q: "How does an agent learn the commands?",
    a: "<code>pb COMMAND --help --json</code> describes any command in a form a model can read, and most commands take <code>--json</code>.",
  },
]
---

<UseCase
  slug="ai-agents"
  name="AI agents"
  title="Remote machines for AI coding agents | Paperboat"
  description="Keep coding agents running on your other machines, with scoped, expiring access and secrets they never see."
  headline="Let your agents work on any machine"
  faq={faq}
  related={["recipes", "env", "exec", "previews"]}
>
  <p slot="lede">Run Claude Code or Codex on the machine with the code and the GPU. It keeps working when you close the laptop, with exactly the access you give it.</p>
  <Term slot="aside" lines={["$ pb connect gpu-box", "ana@gpu-box:~/repo$ claude", "# close the laptop; the agent keeps going", "$ pb connect gpu-box"]} />

  <Beat id="recipe-title" title="One line gives an agent its own machine">
    <p>Put one line in a sandbox template or a CI job. The machine pairs, loads its secrets and opens a preview, set up the way the recipe says.</p>
    <Term
      slot="visual"
      title="agent-3"
      lines={["# in your sandbox or CI job", "$ curl -fsSL \\", `    ${installerBase} \\`, "    | PB_RECIPE=$TOKEN sh", "✓ Paired as agent-3", "✓ Secrets loaded from agent-env", "✓ Preview live for 2 hours"]}
    />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="secrets-title" title="Secrets that never touch the image" flip>
    <p>Keep API keys in a vault. Sandboxes get them when they start, and a command gets them only while it runs.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb env vault create agent-env", "$ pb env set API_KEY --vault agent-env", "# on the sandbox", "$ pb env run -- npm test"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="token-title" title="A token that does one job">
    <p>Tag the machines an agent may use and give it a token for those machines and actions that expires in a week. SSH works with no keys to copy.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb api-token create agent --expires 7d \\", "    --scope-file agent-scope.json", "$ pb ssh build-01"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="exec-title" title="Commands a model can't get wrong" flip>
    <p>Arguments arrive exactly as written, the exit code is the real one, and <code>--json</code> turns it all into events a program can read.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb exec build-01 -- make test", "ok   128 tests passed", "$ echo $?", "0"]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="preview-title" title="See what it built">
    <p>The agent puts its dev server on a link, and you open it from your phone. Every request is kept.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb preview 3000", "Preview ready", `https://quiet-river-lantern-4821.${previewDomain}`]} />
  </Beat>

  <Beat id="watch-title" title="Watch it, or cut it off" flip>
    <p>Record its terminal and replay every step later. If something looks wrong, revoke the machine and it is disconnected at once.</p>
    <Term slot="visual" lines={["$ pb recordings start", "$ pb machine revoke agent-3"]} />
  </Beat>
</UseCase>
